config MESHTASTIC_XEDDSA
	bool "Verify XEdDSA-signed packets"
	default n
	depends on MESHTASTIC_PKI
	select MBEDTLS
	select PSA_WANT_ALG_SHA_512
	help
	  Verify the XEdDSA signatures the reference firmware puts on some
	  broadcasts (position, telemetry, NodeInfo), which are otherwise accepted
	  on the sender id alone. The signature is made with the sender's X25519
	  identity key, so verification needs no extra key material: the key is
	  converted to its Ed25519 form and checked with a standard Ed25519 verify.

	  This is VERIFY ONLY -- this port never signs. That is safe on a mixed
	  mesh because the reference's default policy accepts unsigned traffic;
	  what changes here is that a packet arriving WITH a signature must have a
	  good one.

	  Costs ~19 KB of flash, measured on the XIAO (2026-09-17): the vendored
	  orlp/ed25519 arithmetic is 12.9 KB (src/crypto/ed25519, zlib -- see its
	  PROVENANCE.md), SHA-512 from PSA another 3.3 KB (PKC uses SHA-256, so
	  SHA-512 is not otherwise in the image), and the gate itself ~0.9 KB.
	  Check the headroom before adding this to an image that is already close
	  to the ceiling.

config MESHTASTIC_XEDDSA_SIGN
	bool "Sign our own broadcasts with XEdDSA"
	default n
	depends on MESHTASTIC_XEDDSA
	help
	  Sign the packets this node originates, so peers can authenticate them
	  instead of trusting the sender id. Without this the node verifies
	  others but cannot be verified itself, and a peer running the
	  reference's STRICT policy drops everything we send.

	  ⚠️ COSTS ~38 KB MORE FLASH than verification alone, measured from the
	  objects: the base-point table 30,720 B, sc_muladd 6,548 B (verify uses
	  only sc_reduce), ge_scalarmult_base 264 B, plus this code. Verification
	  links none of it -- the linker garbage-collects the table today.

	  That does NOT fit a XIAO: a class-1 image has ~34 KB of slot left with
	  verification on, and the lockdown variant ~13 KB. This is for the Heltec
	  boards (2 MB slot) until a table-free constant-time base multiplication
	  exists.

	  Do not reach for the vartime path to avoid the table. It is the
	  verifier's, and its running time depends on the scalar -- which during
	  signing is the secret nonce.

	  ⚠️ NEEDS ~2 KB MORE STACK on every thread that originates a packet.
	  Signing happens inside the encoder, on the caller's thread, and those
	  stacks were sized for an encoder that did no curve arithmetic. Enabling
	  this without raising them boot-loops the node: measured on the bench
	  2026-09-17, rzr1 and rzr2 overflowed in meshtastic_nodeinfo and
	  gnss_send. Frames: sign 480 B, derive 240 B, ge_scalarmult_base 512 B,
	  select 176 B, plus hashing. See agents-ooma.35.
